# MyRJ environment variables. Copy to .env.local and fill in what you need.
# Never commit .env.local. Nothing here is required to boot the app: with no keys it opens, the RJ uses
# built-in template lines and your device's own voice, and plays no music until a source is connected.
# Full guide (where each value comes from, redirect URLs, Vercel steps, free-tier limits): docs/FREE-SETUP.md

# ───────────────────────── The $0 setup: these are the only ones you need ─────────────────────────

# ── Google Gemini (RJ scripts, song-language labels, playlist/screenshot import, and the studio voice) ──
# Free tier, no card: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey  → "Create API key"
# Server-side only. Never prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_. Without it the RJ falls back to template lines.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Optional: script model (default gemini-3.5-flash-lite, the roomiest free allowance)
# GEMINI_MODEL=
# Optional: a stronger model tried first for full breaks, e.g. gemini-3.8-flash (small free daily allowance; falls back to GEMINI_MODEL)
# GEMINI_MODEL_FULL=
# Optional: voice models, in order (default gemini-3.8-flash-lite-tts,gemini-3.8-flash-tts). Set GEMINI_TTS=off to never use Gemini for voice.
# GEMINI_TTS_MODELS=
# GEMINI_TTS=

# ── Spotify (optional source; full songs need Spotify Premium) ──
# https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard → Create app → Web API + Web Playback SDK
# Dev-mode apps allow 5 allow-listed users and share a daily quota.
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Must match a Redirect URI in the Spotify dashboard exactly. Use 127.0.0.1, not localhost.
#   local: http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/auth/callback/spotify
#   prod:  https://YOUR-APP.vercel.app/api/auth/callback/spotify
SPOTIFY_REDIRECT_URI=http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/auth/callback/spotify

# ── Google / YouTube (optional source; works without Premium, with YouTube's own ads) ──
# Google Cloud Console → enable "YouTube Data API v3" → OAuth consent screen (External, add yourself
# as a test user) → Credentials → OAuth client ID (Web application).
#   redirect URIs to register: http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/auth/callback/youtube
#                              https://YOUR-APP.vercel.app/api/auth/callback/youtube
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Optional; defaults to <your origin>/api/auth/callback/youtube
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=
# Optional API key (YouTube Data API) for lookups without a signed-in user
# YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# ───────────────────────── Optional voice upgrades (all can stay empty) ─────────────────────────
# Voice order: Gemini → your own voice server → Azure → ElevenLabs → the device's built-in voice.

# ── Your own voice server: free and unlimited, runs on your computer ──
# Any OpenAI-compatible /v1/audio/speech server, e.g. Kokoro-FastAPI or a Piper wrapper.
# Vercel can only reach it through a public HTTPS address (for example a free Cloudflare Tunnel).
# LOCAL_TTS_URL=
# LOCAL_TTS_VOICE=af_heart
# LOCAL_TTS_VOICE_ES=ef_dora
# LOCAL_TTS_VOICE_HI=
# LOCAL_TTS_VOICES=af_heart,am_michael,ef_dora
# LOCAL_TTS_MODEL=kokoro
# LOCAL_TTS_API_KEY=
# LOCAL_TTS_TIMEOUT_MS=15000

# ── Azure Speech (free F0 tier: 0.5M neural characters a month; the account needs a card on file) ──
# Azure Portal → create "Speech service" on the Free F0 tier → Keys and Endpoint
# The Romantic Hindi presets ask for newer "MAI" voices, which are not part of the free allowance:
# on F0 they fall back to the classic Hindi neural voices (or to Gemini when Azure isn't set).
# AZURE_SPEECH_KEY=
# AZURE_SPEECH_REGION=centralindia
# AZURE_TTS_BASE=

# ── ElevenLabs (paid beyond a small monthly credit; not needed) ──
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# ───────────────────────── Not needed for the free personal setup ─────────────────────────

# ── Supabase (optional: accounts, sync across devices, per-user tokens) ──
# Without these the app runs logged-out and keeps settings in the browser (the personal default).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Server only. Secret key. Never expose to the browser.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# Long random string used to encrypt stored refresh tokens: openssl rand -base64 32
# Set once and don't change it, or stored tokens stop working.
# TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ── Claude or another LLM instead of / behind Gemini (both are paid APIs) ──
# Order when several keys are set: Gemini → Claude → OpenAI-compatible → templates.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL_FULL=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL_SENSUAL=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# LLM_API_KEY=
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# How long the script writer may take before the templates step in (ms)
# LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=
